This crate (libspatialite-sys) bundles libspatialite under the `bundled`
Cargo feature (in subsequent commits). When that feature is enabled, the
bundled C source is included in-tree under `vendor/libspatialite-<version>/`
and is statically linked into the resulting binary by `build.rs` via the
`cc` crate.

The crate metadata itself (Cargo.toml, build.rs, src/lib.rs, README.md, etc.)
is dual-licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The bundled libspatialite source
carries its own (separate) licenses described below; static linking
combines those terms with the resulting binary.

================================================================================
libspatialite (bundled under `bundled` feature)
================================================================================

Upstream:       https://www.gaia-gis.it/gaia-sins/libspatialite-sources/
Author:         Alessandro Furieri <a.furieri@lqt.it>
Copyright (C):  2008-2023 Alessandro Furieri and SpatiaLite contributors.

License: triple-licensed under MPL 1.1 / GPL 2.0 / LGPL 2.1.
See `vendor/libspatialite-<version>/COPYING` for the full text of all three
licenses (vendored alongside the source).

This crate links libspatialite STATICALLY when the `bundled` feature is
enabled. Under the LGPL 2.1 option, distributors of resulting binaries are
expected to either:

  (a) provide the recipient with the means to relink the binary against a
      modified libspatialite (typically by shipping the .o files of all
      modules that link directly with libspatialite, or by providing the
      crate consumer's source code so the recipient can rebuild), or
  (b) license the resulting binary under MPL 1.1 or GPL 2.0 instead.

Distributors should consult the LGPL 2.1 text for the exact requirements.
libspatialite-sys itself is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; combining it
with the bundled libspatialite via static linking puts the resulting binary
under the additional terms of one of the libspatialite licenses (per
recipient choice).

================================================================================
GEOS (transitively linked under `bundled` feature)
================================================================================

When the `bundled` feature is enabled, libspatialite is linked against
libgeos / libgeos_c, which is built from C/C++ source by the `geos-src`
crate (declared as a build-dependency by libspatialite-sys at bundled-feature
activation time).

GEOS is licensed under LGPL 2.1. Static linking obligations apply as
described in the libspatialite section above.

================================================================================
PROJ (transitively linked under `bundled` feature)
================================================================================

When the `bundled` feature is enabled, libspatialite is linked against
libproj, which is built from C source by the `proj-sys` crate (declared
as a build-dependency by libspatialite-sys at bundled-feature activation time).

PROJ is licensed under the X/MIT License (a permissive, BSD-style license).

================================================================================
zlib (transitively linked under `bundled` feature)
================================================================================

libspatialite's `gg_relations.c::evalGeosCache` requires zlib's `crc32`.
The `bundled` feature pulls `libz-sys` to build / link a vendored zlib
on all 3 OS (Linux / macOS / Windows). zlib is licensed under the zlib
license (a permissive license).

================================================================================
SQLite headers (header-only at build time)
================================================================================

This crate consumes SQLite headers via `libsqlite3-sys` (`DEP_SQLITE3_INCLUDE`).
SQLite is in the public domain. See https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html .

================================================================================
vcpkg port (under `bundled-vcpkg` feature, Windows MSVC)
================================================================================

The `bundled-vcpkg` feature does not vendor libspatialite source in this
crate. Instead, it relies on the user-provisioned vcpkg installation
(`vcpkg install libspatialite:x64-windows-static-md`). The vcpkg port may
apply patches to upstream libspatialite source; refer to the vcpkg
repository for those patches and their licenses (typically MIT for the
port itself, with the original libspatialite license still applying to the
underlying source).
